    "1778690749e24fd023": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_9nTtAA": {
          "type": "editorial--content",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1200,
            "section_padding": 20,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "heading": "<p>The one with main character energy</p>",
            "heading_size": 46,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_spacing": 10,
            "box_color": "#8b1d22",
            "box_radius": 25,
            "box_padding": 40,
            "box_spacing": 10,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>This is the friend who owns it at every single event, who shows up to a casual dinner looking like it might get photographed. Supreme Power, inspired by Oud for Greatness by Initio, is big, warm and oud-heavy in a way that never once tries to apologize for itself. It is not a fragrance for blending into a room. It is a fragrance for the person who was never trying to blend in anywhere to begin with.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "box_text_size": 22,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.6,
            "paragraph_spacing": 25,
            "subheading": "<p>The one who has had her life together since age 19</p>",
            "subheading_size": 46,
            "subheading_color": "#000000",
            "subheading_spacing": 40,
            "bottom_text": "<p>This is the person who has one signature look, wears it well, and has clearly had her Elle-Woods-channelled life together since she was a teen. <a href=\"/products/luminous-wonder\" title=\"Luminous Wonder\"><strong>Luminous Wonder</strong></a>, inspired by J'Adore by Dior, opens with melon and magnolia, moves into ylang-ylang and jasmine, and settles into vanilla and cedar. It reads as polished without reading as trying, which is exactly the vibe this particular friend has spent years perfecting.</p>",
            "bottom_text_size": 22,
            "bottom_text_color": "#000000",
            "bottom_text_line_height": 1.6
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zVYidR": {
          "type": "editorial--text-section",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The guy who irons his shirts for no reason",
            "heading_size": 50,
            "heading_size_mobile": 32,
            "heading_line_height": 1,
            "heading_color": "#121212",
            "heading_margin_bottom": 50,
            "heading_margin_bottom_mobile": 30,
            "column_1_text": "<p>This is the guy who irons his shirts for no particular occasion and always somehow<br/>looks a little more put together than everyone else in the room. Visionary, inspired by Imagination by Louis Vuitton, opens fresh with citron and bergamot, moves through neroli and ginger, and settles into black tea and warm cedar. It is confident without being loud about it, which tracks for a person who has never once needed to<br/>raise his voice to be heard.</p>",
            "column_2_text": "<p>Oud Maracujá by Maison Crivelli belongs in the same conversation. It regularly sells<br/>for $300 to $375 depending on size, built around an unexpected pairing of passionfruit and oud that quickly built a cult following in niche perfumery circles.<br/>Mirage takes the same passionfruit-and-oud contrast and makes it available at a<br/>fraction of the price, so the pairing that made the original famous is not locked<br/>behind a three-figure price tag.</p>",
            "body_size": 20,
            "body_size_mobile": 14,
            "body_line_height": 1.6,
            "body_color": "#000000",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "column_gap": 60,
            "column_gap_mobile": 30,
            "max_width": 1000,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "padding_top": 60,
            "padding_bottom": 60,
            "padding_horizontal": 40,
            "padding_top_mobile": 40,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
            "padding_horizontal_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_9nTtAA",
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zVYidR"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
    "blocks_jgTJWD": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_kVmwE7": {
          "type": "editorial--staggered-typography",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "line_1_text": "Timeless Grace",
            "line_1_alignment": "left",
            "line_1_offset": 300,
            "line_2_text": "vs",
            "line_2_alignment": "center",
            "line_2_offset": 0,
            "line_3_text": "Coco Mademoiselle by Chanel:",
            "line_3_alignment": "right",
            "line_3_offset": -40,
            "body_text": "<p>Coco Mademoiselle is the benchmark for a certain kind of feminine fragrance. Clean, grown-up, and immediately recognisable. It has been the top-selling women's perfume in the UK and US for years. The EDP retails at around $160 for 100ml and it earns that position consistently.</p><p><strong>Timeless Grace</strong> opens with the same fresh orange and bergamot, develops through jasmine and rose, and settles into a warm patchouli base that wears throughout the day. The comparison test here produced the closest result of the three: on dry-down, both fragrances sat in the same warm, clean territory. The original has a very slight additional depth in the base that reflects the higher concentration of raw materials, but it is a difference you would only notice if you were specifically looking for it.<br/><br/>At around $20 versus $160, Timeless Grace makes a compelling case for anyone who loves the Coco Mademoiselle profile but wants to wear it every day without the creeping sense that they should be saving it for something more significant.</p>",
            "line_1_size": 44,
            "line_2_size": 85,
            "line_3_size": 44,
            "body_size": 22,
            "line_2_margin_top": 30,
            "line_3_margin_top": 4,
            "header_spacing": 40,
            "body_max_width": 1000,
            "section_padding_top": 60,
            "section_padding_bottom": 60,
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "text_color": "#121212"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_kVmwE7"
      ],
      "name": "Staggered typography",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "17786893180b60ea14": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_c88e324_m8PFU4": {
          "type": "editorial--section",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "container_width": 1200,
            "left_column_width": 40,
            "right_column_width": 60,
            "column_gap": 40,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "Where The Differences actually Show Up",
            "heading_font": "serif",
            "heading_size": 56,
            "mobile_heading_size": 40,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_indent": 10,
            "mobile_heading_indent": 40,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/magnific_luxury-perfume-comparison_74h5S6MJAL_jpg.jpg",
            "image_max_width": 600,
            "heading_image_gap": 4,
            "mobile_heading_image_gap": 25,
            "body_text": "<p>Across all our tests, the differences between inspired fragrances and originals came down to three things.<br/><br/><strong>Concentration of raw materials</strong>. Designer houses use extremely high concentrations of expensive ingredients. The originals have a certain richness in the base that reflects this. A well-made inspired fragrance gets close, but the very finest nuances of a $300 bottle are sometimes in those base notes, and it is worth knowing that going in.<br/><br/><strong>Projection in the opening</strong>. Top notes on the originals tend to radiate a little further, particularly in the first half an hour after applying. This matters if you are spraying in an elevator and want to make an immediate impression. It matters less if you are wearing something all day for yourself.<br/><br/><strong>Longevity on dry skin</strong>. Both perform significantly better on moisturised skin. On dry skin, the originals do have a slight edge in staying power. The fix is twelve seconds of moisturiser before you spray. After that, the gap closes considerably.</p>",
            "body_font": "system_ui_n4",
            "body_size": 24,
            "mobile_body_size": 16,
            "body_color": "#000000",
            "paragraph_spacing": 30,
            "mobile_paragraph_spacing": 15,
            "text_vertical_offset": 10,
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "padding_top": 100,
            "padding_bottom": 100,
            "horizontal_padding": 40,
            "mobile_padding_top": 60,
            "mobile_padding_bottom": 60,
            "mobile_horizontal_padding": 20,
            "mobile_gap": 30
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_c88e324_m8PFU4"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
    "blocks_NgyNz4": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_qVFqqX": {
          "type": "editorial--content",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1200,
            "section_padding": 20,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "heading": "<p>The guy who irons his shirts for no reason</p>",
            "heading_size": 50,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_spacing": 10,
            "box_color": "#8b1d22",
            "box_radius": 25,
            "box_padding": 40,
            "box_spacing": 10,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>This is the guy who irons his shirts for no particular occasion and always somehow looks a little more put together than everyone else in the room. Visionary, inspired by Imagination by Louis Vuitton, opens fresh with citron and bergamot, moves through neroli and ginger, and settles into black tea and warm cedar. It is confident without being loud about it, which tracks for a person who has never once needed to raise his voice to be heard.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#ffffff",
